[4.131701, "o", " wheeltap scan demo\r\n# Wheeltap\r\n\r\nNo findings. Scanned 1 file, 73 lines.\r\nexit 0\r\n\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m # the same program, with a withdraw instruction added\r\n\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m wheeltap scan demo\r\n# Wheeltap\r\n\r\n**2 findings** in 1 file, 98 lines.\r\n\r\n| Severity | Count |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| critical | 1 |\r\n| high | 1 |\r\n\r\n## Critical\r\n\r\n### `WT001` lib.rs:74\r\n\r\n`Withdraw.authority` is verified by a `has_one` constraint but is never required to sign, and no account in `Withdraw` signs at all. The constraint proves which account this is; it does not prove the holder authorised anything. Public keys are public, so any caller can pass this one.\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n    pub authority: AccountInfo<'info>,\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Fix.** Type the account as `Signer<'info>`. If it must stay an `AccountInfo`, require the signature explicitly with `#[account(signer)]` or `constraint = authority.is_signer`.\r\n\r\n<sub>critical \u00b7 confidence high \u00b7 `Withdraw.authority` \u00b7 id `7cd936585971af1f`</sub>\r\n\r\n<sub>[reference](https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/signer-auth) \u00b7 [reference](https://github.com/coral-xyz/sealevel-attacks)</sub>\r\n\r\n## High\r\n\r\n### `WT003` lib.rs:35\r\n\r\n`vault.balance -= amount` in `withdraw` uses `-=` on a value that holds funds. In a release build this wraps silently rather than failing.\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n        vault.balance -= amount;\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Fix.** Use `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` and return an error on overflow, or `saturating_*` where clamping is the intended behaviour. Alternatively set `overflow-checks = true` under `[profile.release]`, which turns wrapping into a panic and silences this rule.\r\n\r\n<sub>high \u00b7 confidence medium \u00b7 `vault::withdraw` \u00b7 id `321cce722e45acd9`</sub>\r\n\r\n<sub>"]
